WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:06.300
The Harry Potter series has been a consistent
source of magic for more than two decades.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.600
"WICKED!"

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.800
But not all of the silver screen adaptations
of J.K.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.940
Rowling's works have turned out as well as
others.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:18.360
From pacing issues to distracting book-to-screen
inconsistencies to moments of shoddy direction,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.740
some of the films simply don't measure up
to the rest.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.000
So, let's walk through all of the Harry Potter
films, starting with the best and counting

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.460
down to find out which of them is officially
the worst Harry Potter movie ever made.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.460
Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.890
There was the Harry Potter franchise before
Prisoner of Azkaban, and there was the Harry

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.839
Potter franchise after.

00:00:38.839 --> 00:00:43.489
Director Alfonso Cuarón brought more than
just fresh eyes to the series' third installment.

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:47.719
He also brought a whole new perspective to
the magical franchise by grounding it in humanity.

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:52.040
Cuarón had the benefit of the prior films'
world-building already in place, of course.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.170
But he also brought a great deal of style
and gravity to the story and helped to darken

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.289
the mood and ramp up the sense of true danger
in the movies just in time.

00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:04.930
Even from the film's opening moments, the
film seems more alive than before, with performances

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.410
that rang a little more true.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:10.780
The energy of the movie is electric, and draws
us into Harry's life in ways the first two

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.030
films hadn't.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.560
That's why the Dementors' attacks on him are
so frightening and why Sirius Black's character

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.890
arc is utterly compelling to watch.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:23.020
Not only did the film bring wonder back to
Hogwarts, it also fundamentally altered the

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.729
direction of the franchise and became a benchmark
for the entire series to follow.

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:29.679
Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix

00:01:29.679 --> 00:01:33.850
By the time the fifth Harry Potter film came
along, the series was starting to barrel towards

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:35.240
its endgame.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.679
Voldemort has already returned, and lives
are being lost as a result.

00:01:38.679 --> 00:01:42.820
The days of caring about house points and
sneaking through the restricted section are

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.060
certainly over for Harry and his pals.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.189
And in addition to the looming dangers of
the outside, Order of the Phoenix really brings

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:54.310
it home when Dolores Umbridge ushers the authoritarianism
rising within the Ministry of Magic to the

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.060
halls of Hogwarts.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.590
Harry and those loyal to Dumbledore must band
together in secret to survive her reign, and

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:05.219
yet, it feels like a hopeless endeavor and
causes a sense of dread that's very real for

00:02:05.219 --> 00:02:06.530
audiences at home.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.670
Unlike many of its predecessors, Order of
the Phoenix never feels overwhelmed by its

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:11.910
narrative ambition.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:16.390
It plugs along at a brisk pace, covering the
bases - including the series' first full-on

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:20.870
wizard fight - and delivers one of the series'
biggest emotional payoffs in its harrowing

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.870
final moments.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.140
It was director David Yates' first foray into
the franchise, and it's easy to see why they

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.800
kept him around after this movie struck so
many high notes.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.690
Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:36.100
In many ways, Half-Blood Prince actually beats
Order of the Phoenix on the dramatic front.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:39.630
The film's impact is bolstered by a devastating
third act.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:43.610
The film finds Harry and friends continuing
to fight the good fight while unraveling the

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:48.430
deep, dark secret that's made Voldemort all
but immortal, and it's a thrill to watch as

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.800
the stakes get raised to immeasurably scary
levels.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.850
Structured more as a pulpy detective story
than a magical adventure tale, Half-Blood

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:59.930
Prince is the one film in the series that
can be qualified as a genuine slow-burner.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.900
It introduces the element of the horcruxes,
of Snape's ulterior motives, and decimates

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.660
any sense of safety that might've remained
before.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.310
Half-Blood Prince may test your patience with
its pacing, and certain creative liberties

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.700
in the plot might irk Potter purists.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:18.680
But it does deliver on the drama and nimbly
sets into motion the series' big finish.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.501
Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows Part
2

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:25.930
Due to the final book's length and density,
Warner Bros. decided to split the last installment

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:29.340
of the series in two films with the hopes
that David Yates and his team could give the

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:34.470
franchise the send-off it deserved -- and
earn an extra helping of profits, of course.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:39.180
Despite a wobbly start with Part 1, Yates
managed to achieve a fitting end with Deathly

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.380
Hallows Part 2.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.960
The closing chapter covers Harry, Hermione,
and Ron's desperate search for Voldemort's

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:49.800
horcruxes, Snape's surprising history, the
epic Battle of Hogwarts, and Harry's fateful

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.180
showdown with the last heir of Slytherin.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:56.780
It's a lot of action and drama to sift through
for one film, and some fans have expressed

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.970
disappointment with the way the final showdown
between Harry and the Dark Lord plays out.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.290
But with the many smaller battles and moments
of epic heroism on display in the end, Deathly

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:10.040
Hallows still ends with a bang … as long
as you turn it off before the silly epilogue,

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.040
that is.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.310
Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.310
J.K.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:18.220
Rowling decided to travel back to the past
for the series' next cinematic adventure.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.260
Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them, which
she scripted, follows the little-known character

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:28.220
Newt Scamander in 1920s New York as he inadvertently
unleashes a bevy of magical creatures into

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.250
the muggle realm.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:33.120
The Big Apple proves to be a welcome change
of scenery for Rowling's world.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.720
Free from the world of O.W.L. exams and teen
angst, the more grown-up tale of wizards wandering

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.500
the world feels fresh and offers a new lens
through which to view the magical realm.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.710
The film is filled with action, adventure,
and frightening foes, but the human element

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.470
of the story is front and center, which makes
it a little less draining than some of its

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:51.560
predecessors.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:56.590
That said, it suffers from some very slow
moments and a sense of directionlessness that

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.460
makes the film feel very choppy.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.400
And with the forthcoming sequel, The Crimes
of Grindelwald, just around the corner, we

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.490
can expect this sub-series to start building
back up to an all-out war sooner rather than

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.650
later, which might make Fantastic Beasts 2
feel formulaic.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.210
Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows Part
1

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.030
There are a lot of things that do work about
Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.030
1.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:23.030
For starters, it successfully sets up the
big finish and offers some moments of emotional

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:26.120
evocation that hadn't yet been seen in the
series.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:31.010
It also separates the trio from everything
they've ever known and puts the whole horcrux

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.889
hunt on the fast track.

00:05:32.889 --> 00:05:37.360
However, despite the film's stylish scenery
and some gutting performances by the leading

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.280
trio of cast mates, the film is pretty boring
and seems to unnecessarily eat up screen time

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:46.820
with characters sitting around, just to justify
making the final installment a two-parter.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:51.510
The animated mini-movie and Dobby's last stand
were stand-out moments of the whole series,

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:56.389
but Deathly Hallows Part 1 could have still
been reduced to half an hour or so and tacked

00:05:56.389 --> 00:06:00.360
onto the following film, and fans wouldn't
have missed out on much.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.260
"True, every word."

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.139
Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire

00:06:05.139 --> 00:06:09.510
After cheating death for three straight years,
Harry's fourth year at Hogwarts proved to

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.480
be his most perilous yet.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.400
Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire finds
the tortured teen wizard competing as the

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:20.480
youngest-ever contestant in the Tri-wizard
Tournament, and facing down the murderous

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.800
dark lord himself, Voldemort.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.700
Although the tournament setting does offer
a nice contrast between the kids' fanciful

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:31.230
youth with the true grimness of the world
that surrounds them, the movie also suffers

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.210
from some pretty cringe-worthy acting.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:36.250
"Harry, take my body back, will you.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.300
Take my body back to my father."

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:44.440
It also fails to find nuance in the secondary
characters, like Cedric Diggory and Cho Chang,

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.700
which means their emotional arcs fall flat.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:50.940
The best part of the film is when Harry and
Voldemort finally come face to face, but the

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:55.389
whole encounter is limited to just a few minutes
and feels like an afterthought that's overshadowed

00:06:55.389 --> 00:06:57.690
by far less important drama.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.480
Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:03.560
Credit is due to Christopher Columbus for
constructing a beautiful vision of Hogwarts

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.280
and the intricacies of magic found in J.K.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.870
Rowling's story in Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's
Stone.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:13.310
And, ultimately, his casting choices for most
of the characters would prove to pay off big

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.400
time in the long run.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:19.550
However, with the kids being so young in the
earliest installment, their line deliveries

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:23.980
leave something to be desired, and the film
feels more like a cheery Disney movie than

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:27.540
the start of a long, hard battle for the Boy
Who Lived.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:32.710
With its three-headed beasts, shape-shifting
professors, flying brooms, and a larger-than-life

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:37.980
chess match, though, there's still some major
magic to behold in Harry's first year at Hogwarts.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:42.300
In the end, this first installment of the
landmark franchise is just magical enough

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:46.800
to keep your attention, but it's also a bit
of a snoozer on repeat viewings.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.729
Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets

00:07:48.729 --> 00:07:53.550
Chris Columbus's return to adapt the second
Harry Potter installment, Chamber of Secrets,

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.699
is even less impressive than the first.

00:07:55.699 --> 00:08:00.479
Sure, the film offers up a genuine sense of
discovery, and even danger, to the famed school

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:06.020
surrounded by whomping willows, spider-filled
forests, and the titular Chamber of Secrets.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:10.330
And all of this happens just as Harry and
friends begin to unravel the dark and twisted

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.120
history of Tom Riddle.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:16.110
Unfortunately, Chamber of Secrets still sees
its stars struggling to find their way as

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:21.169
actors, while the director misses big moments
with poor tone and pacing choices as well.

00:08:21.169 --> 00:08:25.320
There are no bad installments to the Harry
Potter film series, of course.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:30.100
But with this one side-stepping so many potential
power punches written into the book's storyline,

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:33.360
well, it's arguably the least magical of them
all.

00:08:36.169 --> 00:08:37.320
Thanks for watching!

00:08:37.329 --> 00:08:39.829
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:39.829 --> 00:08:41.849
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

